# Architecture Rules

Before implementing any feature:

* Audit the project.
* Reuse existing components.
* Reuse existing database tables.
* Reuse existing services.
* Reuse navigation.
* Avoid duplicate code.

Never redesign approved functionality unless instructed.

---

# Business Rules

* Customers may have multiple sales.
* A sale contains one or more sale items.
* Payments may be partial.
* Customer balances are calculated, never manually edited.
* Products are a catalogue only in Version 1.
* Expenses are independent records.
* Financial actions require confirmation.
* Every financial action generates an audit record.
* Every important event generates a timeline event.

---

# Rules Engine

All financial actions must pass through a central Rules Engine.

The Rules Engine validates:

* Required fields.
* Duplicate customers.
* Payment amounts.
* Credit calculations.
* Invalid dates.
* Business rules.

No financial record bypasses the Rules Engine.

